cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or write about Meteora, please cite it as below."
title: "Meteora: a reverb computed from a real landscape"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Eriksen
    given-names: Trent
    alias: Grashopr
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/Grashopr-888/meteora-releases/releases"
url: "https://grashopr-888.github.io/current-projects/projects/meteora/"
date-released: 2026-11-06
version: 0.3.0
abstract: >-
  A free reverb plug-in for macOS (VST3 and Standalone) whose space is computed from open terrain data of
  Meteora, Greece, with two movable microphones, weather-dependent air absorption, and a listener that can
  suggest or make changes to the settings. Closed-source freeware; released as a research preview for
  ADC 2026, Bristol.
keywords:
  - reverb
  - audio plug-in
  - geometric acoustics
  - open data
  - Meteora
